From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:52:14 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: let a P010 queue allocate its two buffers

VIDIOC_REQBUFS fails with ENOMEM for P010 at any size and count, while
NV12 works. The P010 rendered pool has two slots, and queue_setup limits
the queue to the pool. vb2 allocates at least min_queued_buffers + 1
buffers, three with ISP_MIN_FRAMES, so __vb2_queue_alloc gets two and
vb2_core_reqbufs returns -ENOMEM. P010 has failed this way since it was
added; the IOVA allocator and the DART window are not involved (the two
buffers map fine and are torn down again).

Set the queue minimum from the format whenever S_FMT changes it, which
only happens with no buffers: one queued buffer starts a P010 stream, so
vb2 needs two. NV12 keeps ISP_MIN_FRAMES.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

(cherry picked from commit e84b0b5faedac230434f864a77372ad579625961)
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-v4l2.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-v4l2.c
index 87f28169e0..ad79c4b1fb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-v4l2.c
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@
 #define ISP_BUFFER_TIMEOUT msecs_to_jiffies(1500)
 #define ISP_STRIDE_ALIGNMENT 64
 
+static void isp_vb2_set_min_buffers(struct apple_isp *isp);
+
 /* Capture rates offered to userspace, in frames per second */
 static const unsigned int isp_frame_rates[] = { 30, 25, 24, 20, 15 };
 
@@ -849,6 +851,7 @@ static int isp_vidioc_set_format(struct file *file, void *fh,
 	isp_get_sp_pix_format(isp, f, fmt);
 
 	isp->vbq.type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE;
+	isp_vb2_set_min_buffers(isp);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1039,6 +1042,22 @@ static void isp_free_meta_surfaces(struct apple_isp *isp)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * vb2 allocates at least min_queued_buffers + 1 buffers, and the queue may
+ * hold no more than the rendered pool (isp_vb2_queue_setup()). The P010 pool
+ * has two slots, so a P010 stream starts with one queued buffer; otherwise
+ * REQBUFS can never get the three buffers vb2 asks for and fails with ENOMEM.
+ * Only called while the queue has no buffers.
+ */
+static void isp_vb2_set_min_buffers(struct apple_isp *isp)
+{
+	struct vb2_queue *vbq = &isp->vbq;
+
+	vbq->min_queued_buffers = min_t(unsigned int, ISP_MIN_FRAMES,
+					 isp_num_rendered(isp) - 1);
+	vbq->min_reqbufs_allocation = vbq->min_queued_buffers + 1;
+}
+
 static int isp_vb2_queue_init(struct apple_isp *isp)
 {
 	struct vb2_queue *vbq = &isp->vbq;
